  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At 42 rue Thiers, just steps from the old port of Saint-Raphaël, Moelleuses & Persillées showcases bistronomic cuisine centred on aged meats — Black Angus, Wagyu, Kobe — alongside seafood, and is listed in the Gault&Millau guide. Dogs are allowed, on both the air-conditioned indoor and outdoor terraces — and this is more than mere tolerance: the establishment's official website (mpstraphael.fr) has a page explicitly titled "Chic restaurant with dogs allowed, right in central Saint-Raphaël", a top-tier official confirmation.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The restaurant also offers vegetarian options and a welcome designed for children, making it a versatile address for the whole family, dog included. Open 7 days a week according to the official website. Parking is available nearby to make arriving easier.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if you're travelling with a good appetite and a well-behaved dog under the table, this is one of the best addresses in the area for meat.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The old port of Saint-Raphaël is right nearby, pleasant for a walk before or after the meal.</p>
